<statement>
<p>
	22 has 2, 11 as prime factors and sum of digits 2 + 2 = 2 + 1 + 1 sum of digits in prime factors 588 has 2, 2, 3, 7, 7 as prime factors, and sum of digits 5 + 8 + 8 = 2 + 2 + 3 + 7 + 7 sum of digits in prime factors
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>number</pf> (1 x 1) integer — positive integer.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>result</pf> (1 x 1) number — true if <pf>number</pf> is Smith. false otherwise.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Code this by calling your</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>HW2P6_num_2_digits</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>and</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>HW3P5_prime_factors</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>functions within this function.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>You may use MATLAB's</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>sum</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>function.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

<p>
	Examples:
<program>
	<code>
		is_smith(11010)
		0 (logical)
		is_smith(958)
		1 (logical)
	</code>
</program>
</p>
</statement>
